{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-330831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}$ for $s>0$, find the Laplace transform of\n$g(t)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{τ}^{3}\\,\\text{d}τ$\nfor $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(t)={t}^{3}.$ Thus, for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =L{f(t)} \\\\  & =L{{t}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3!}{{s}^{3+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the integral identity above, we have that for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{g(t)} & =L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}{τ}^{3}\\,\\text{d}τ} \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{s}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "279c2a1df0bdee3c31bfce5fcb8522ea73c02ce8cfebfcb28687ef2b1bf9da9c"} {"question" "q-330831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{24}{{s}^{4}}"] ["math" "\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{{s}^{4}}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{{s}^{5}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{6}{{s}^{5}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $L{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a}$ for $s>a$, find the Laplace transform of\n$g(t)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{4τ}\\,\\text{d}τ$\nfor $s>4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(t)={e}^{4t}.$ Thus, for $s>4,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =L{f(t)} \\\\  & =L{{e}^{4t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the integral identity above, we have that for $s>4,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{g(t)} & =L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{4τ}\\,\\text{d}τ} \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330825" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "279c2a1df0bdee3c31bfce5fcb8522ea73c02ce8cfebfcb28687ef2b1bf9da9c"} {"question" "q-330825" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330825" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{s(s-4)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{s-4}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{s-4}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{s-4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330825" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{s(s-4)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t)}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}$ for $s>0$, find the Laplace transform of\n$g(t)={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2τ)\\,\\text{d}τ$\nfor $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t).$ Thus, for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =L{f(t)} \\\\  & =L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the integral identity above, we have that for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{g(t)} & =L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2τ)\\,\\text{d}τ} \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "279c2a1df0bdee3c31bfce5fcb8522ea73c02ce8cfebfcb28687ef2b1bf9da9c"} {"question" "q-330835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+4}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+4}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $L{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a}$ for $s>a$, find the Laplace transform of\n$g(t)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-3τ}\\,\\text{d}τ$\nfor $s>-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(t)={e}^{-3t}.$ Thus, for $s>-3,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =L{f(t)} \\\\  & =L{{e}^{-3t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the integral identity above, we have that for $s>-3,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{g(t)} & =L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-3τ}\\,\\text{d}τ} \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s(s+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "279c2a1df0bdee3c31bfce5fcb8522ea73c02ce8cfebfcb28687ef2b1bf9da9c"} {"question" "q-330826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{s(s+3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{s+3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{s+3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{s+3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{s(s+3)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t)}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}$ for $s>0$, find the Laplace transform of\n$g(t)={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3τ)\\,\\text{d}τ$\nfor $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$ Thus, for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =L{f(t)} \\\\  & =L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the integral identity above, we have that for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{g(t)} & =L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3τ)\\,\\text{d}τ} \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{s({s}^{2}+9)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "279c2a1df0bdee3c31bfce5fcb8522ea73c02ce8cfebfcb28687ef2b1bf9da9c"} {"question" "q-330834" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330834" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3}{s({s}^{2}+9)}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{{s}^{2}+9}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330834" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{s({s}^{2}+9)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{24}{{s}^{6}},\\,s>0\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{24}{{s}^{6}}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{F(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4!}{{s}^{4+1}}} \\\\  & ={t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{G(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{F(s)}{s}} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{τ}^{4}\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "279c2a1df0bdee3c31bfce5fcb8522ea73c02ce8cfebfcb28687ef2b1bf9da9c"} {"question" "q-330843" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330843" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{24}{{t}^{5}}"] ["math" "\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{{t}^{6}}{30}"] ["math" "{t}^{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330843" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{720}{{s}^{8}},\\,s>0\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{720}{{s}^{8}}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{720}{{s}^{7}}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{F(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{720}{{s}^{7}}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{6!}{{s}^{6+1}}} \\\\  & ={t}^{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{G(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{F(s)}{s}} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{τ}^{6}\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{7}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "279c2a1df0bdee3c31bfce5fcb8522ea73c02ce8cfebfcb28687ef2b1bf9da9c"} {"question" "q-330845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{720}{{t}^{7}}"] ["math" "\\frac{{t}^{6}}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{{t}^{7}}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{{t}^{8}}{56}"] ["math" "{t}^{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{t}^{7}}{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s({s}^{2}+4)},\\,s>0\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t)}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s({s}^{2}+4)}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+4}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t)}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{F(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{G(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{F(s)}{s}} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "279c2a1df0bdee3c31bfce5fcb8522ea73c02ce8cfebfcb28687ef2b1bf9da9c"} {"question" "q-330838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{4}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s-5)},\\,s>5\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\text{ }s>a.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s-5)}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{1}{s-5}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{F(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-5}} \\\\  & ={e}^{5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{G(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{F(s)}{s}} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{5τ}\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5τ}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{5t}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "279c2a1df0bdee3c31bfce5fcb8522ea73c02ce8cfebfcb28687ef2b1bf9da9c"} {"question" "q-330849" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330849" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{5}(1-{e}^{5t})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{5t}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{t}-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{s-5}"] ["math" "{e}^{5t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-330849" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{5t}-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-327935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s({s}^{2}+{\\pi }^{2})},\\,s>0\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t)}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-327935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s({s}^{2}+{\\pi }^{2})}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+{\\pi }^{2}}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t)}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{F(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+{\\pi }^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{L}^{-1}{\\frac{\\pi }{{s}^{2}+{\\pi }^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{G(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{F(s)}{s}} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-327935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "279c2a1df0bdee3c31bfce5fcb8522ea73c02ce8cfebfcb28687ef2b1bf9da9c"} {"question" "q-327935" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-327935" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t))"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-327935" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t))"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-331084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we wish to find $L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ}$ given $L{f(t)}=F(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.Let $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ={{field-1}}\\,{|}_{0}^{t}=A(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ}=L{A(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & ⇒ & du={A}^{′}(t)\\text{ }dt \\\\ dv={{field-3}} & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({{field-4}}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=$ $0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-5}}\\,\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={{field-6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-331084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ & =A(τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =A(t)-A(0) \\\\  & =A(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ} & =L{A(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & \\,⇒\\, & du={A}^{′}(t)\\,dt \\\\ dv={e}^{-st}\\,dt & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A(0)=0$ and $\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ we have $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=0$ and\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot F(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/state.json" "file_sha256" "284e7ca9146e141d4785aec462536df2a2b7db0a282f39f8675e2fbbfef157d9"} {"question" "q-331084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073261/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "279c2a1df0bdee3c31bfce5fcb8522ea73c02ce8cfebfcb28687ef2